## Pre-Transfer Validation

Before transferring to the highside, verify:

- [ ] `rhis_disconnected_manifest.yml` exists in the bundle directory
- [ ] `copy_rhis_to_transfer_media.sh` will verify checksums — review any failures before transfer
- [ ] All required ISOs are available at the highside (see above)
- [ ] Vault password has been communicated via a separate trusted channel
- [ ] Transfer media has sufficient capacity (see Stage 1 output)
- [ ] Highside satellite host is provisioned with RHEL and accessible via SSH

---

## Stage 2 — Copy to Transfer Media

Once transfer media is mounted, run:

```bash
./copy_rhis_to_transfer_media.sh \
    --bundle-dir {{ _bundle_path }} \
    --pulp-export-dir {{ _pulp_path }} \
    --media-path <mount_point>
```

---

## Highside Import Sequence

After mounting transfer media on the highside provisioner:

1. **Load the container image:**
   ```bash
   podman load -i <media>/rhis_transfer_*/container/rhis-provisioner_*.tar
   ```

2. **Extract the inventory:**
   ```bash
   tar -xzf <media>/rhis_transfer_*/inventory/rhis_inventory_*.tar.gz -C /rhis/vars/
   ```

3. **Copy `content_imports.yml` into your discosatellite host_vars:**
   ```bash
   cp <media>/rhis_transfer_*/content_imports.yml \
       /rhis/vars/host_vars/<discosatellite_hostname>/
   ```

4. **Upload each highside manifest from `manifests/`** to the appropriate
   discosatellite host_vars `files/manifests/` directory.

5. **Run the import:**
   ```bash
   ./build_sat_disconnected_import.sh \
       --bundle-path <media>/rhis_transfer_*/ \
       --sshuser ansiblerunner
   ```

---

## Notes

- AAP installation files (RPMs and setup bundle) are included in the Library export
  via the AAP content views — no separate AAP ISO required.
- SCAP tailoring files are included in the inventory archive.
- The `rhis_disconnected_manifest.yml` checksums cover bundle artifacts only,
  not the Pulp library export chunks (those are validated by Satellite during import).
